# V2 Database Schema

## Source of Truth

DDL lives in `v2/` — run order per `v2/README.md` (`00_helpers.sql` first, then `01`–`08`). Schema changes require a new numbered SQL file in `v2/`.

## Table Naming

Always use `v2_*` prefix. Never create `offerings_v2`, `franchises_v2`, or `instance_v2` style names. Do not extend `@/lib/db-v2.ts` (deprecated old table names).

## C-end vs Admin naming

**Canonical mapping:** see always-applied rule `product-hierarchy.mdc`.

Summary: Web Campus = `v2_franchise`; Web Location = `v2_campus`; Web Program = `v2_category`; Web Activity = `v2_program`; Web Session = `v2_instance`. Session card title = `v2_offering.name` (offering is not a Web nav level).

## Entity Hierarchy

- **Config**: `v2_offering_type` — `offering_schema` / `instance_schema` drive dynamic fields
- **Global**: `v2_category`, `v2_offering`
- **Franchise**: `v2_franchise`, `v2_franchise_category_map`, `v2_campus`
- **Operations**: `v2_program`, `v2_instance` (user purchase target)
- `v2_instance.featured` (boolean, default `false`) — marks an instance for featured/recommended display on the C-end
- `v2_instance.amilia_link` (text, nullable) — external Amilia enrollment URL; C-end instance detail uses it for “Enroll now” when set (migration `11_v2_instance_amilia_link.sql`)

## Schema-Driven Fields

- `v2_offering.type_config_data` ← `offering_schema`; flatten nested keys (e.g. `pricing.base_price`) to table columns on write
- `v2_instance.instance_data_ext` ← `instance_schema`; object groups (`schedule`, `capacity_price`) derive row columns (`start_date`, `max_students`, etc.)
- Validate against schema before insert/update; display via `@/lib/instance-schema.ts` (see `admin/instance/v2/route.ts`)
- **C-end date labels**: format `v2_instance.start_date` / `end_date` (DATE / `YYYY-MM-DD`) with `@/lib/format-calendar-date.ts` — show the stored calendar day for all users; do not use `new Date(isoDateOnly)` or viewer timezone for display

## Status & Integrity

- Offering status: `draft` | `published` | `suspended` | `archived`
- Instance status: `scheduled` | `ongoing` | `completed` | `cancelled`
- Program: category must be subscribed by franchise (`v2_franchise_category_map`)
- Instance: offering.category_id must match program.category_id; campus must belong to program's franchise

## Query Pattern

```typescript
supabaseAdmin.from("v2_instance").select(`
  *,
  program:v2_program(id, name, franchise:v2_franchise(code, name)),
  offering:v2_offering(id, name, offering_type:v2_offering_type(instance_schema))
`)
```

Use `supabaseAdmin`; copy joins from `src/app/api/admin/*/v2/` routes. Treat `PGRST116` as not-found.
## Non-Catalog Tables

Auth/users, enrollments (`instance_enrollments`), Stripe are separate — `v2_resource` tables follow existing API routes, not `v2/` DDL.
